      <p class="rte-aeo-label">Quick Answer</p>
      <p class="rte-aeo-text">
        In 2026, your retirement tax bill depends on <strong class="rte-gold">Provisional Income</strong> — your total income plus 50% of Social Security. If Provisional Income exceeds <strong class="rte-gold">$25,000 (single)</strong> or <strong class="rte-gold">$32,000 (joint)</strong>, up to 50–85% of your Social Security becomes taxable. All IRA and pension withdrawals are taxed as ordinary income. Seniors 65+ receive an extra standard deduction of <strong class="rte-gold">$1,650 (married) or $2,050 (unmarried)</strong>, reducing taxable income.
      </p>
      <p class="rte-qa-footer" style="font-size: 0.85rem; color: #E8F4F1; margin: 0.75rem 0 0; padding-top: 0.5rem; border-top: 1px solid rgba(255,255,255,0.2);">
